11
00:00:37.103 --> 00:00:40.807
call plan action
alignment is through inline evaluation.

12
00:00:40.940 --> 00:00:43.910
Inline evaluation provides
real time feedback

13
00:00:43.910 --> 00:00:47.380
so that the agent can actually understand
how well it's performing.

14
00:00:47.547 --> 00:00:50.050
For example, when it does a research step.

15
00:00:50.050 --> 00:00:54.888
The agent executer Can be provided
with an evaluation score and explanation

16
00:00:54.988 --> 00:00:58.925
to see if the research is missing
key details before it can move on.

17
00:00:59.092 --> 00:01:02.695
The agent can then use that information
to better choose its next action.

18
00:01:02.862 --> 00:01:05.732
You might also choose
to improve your agent's performance

19
00:01:05.732 --> 00:01:09.069
by doing things like tuning the retriever
or trying different models.

20
00:01:09.235 --> 00:01:13.506
Last, you should always validate your
improvements through offline evaluations.

